WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
Take one faithful, long-term
relationship between two adults.

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:10.500
Natural law, Kant, situation ethics and
utilitarianism can all be asked to judge

3
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:11.250
it.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.990
Some have condemned what others approve,
and critics say some old conclusions

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.960
were products of their age.

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.360
So why do four theories look at the same
relationship and reach such different

7
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.660
answers?

8
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.270
In this mission, you'll see how
situation ethics judges premarital sex,

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.310
adultery and same-sex relationships.

10
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:36.380
Then you'll weigh up whether ethical
theories are useful in sexual ethics at all.

11
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.250
Your mission: work out why four theories
give one relationship such different

12
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.030
answers.
